SUMMARY:Toronto Summer Music Festival:  Timothy Chooi (1714 Strad)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n{ This concert is **SOLD-OUT** }\n\nWe
  will attend 3 concerts at this year's Toronto Summer Music Festival.\n\nY
 ou could use the 10% off promo code for tickets ($30-$80)\n\n**Timothy Cho
 oi\, violin**\n**Jon Kimura Parker\, piano**\n\nVitali: Chaconne in G mino
 r\nGluck: “Mélodie” from *Orfeo ed Euridice*\nJohn Corigliano: *The R
 ed Violin Caprices*\nFranck: Sonata in A Major for Violin and Piano\n\nA c
 elebration of one of the most iconic voices in violin history\, featuring 
 **Timothy Chooi performing on the legendary 1714 “Dolphin” Stradivariu
 s\,** famously played by Jascha Heifetz\, alongside the incomparable Jon K
 imura Parker. From the electrifying drama of the Vitali Chaconne and the e
 legance of Gluck’s Mélodie\, to the high-wire brilliance of Corigliano
 ’s *Red Violin Caprices*\, the first half captures the fire\, precision\
 , and charisma that defined the Heifetz legacy. After intermission\, Franc
 k’s timeless Sonata brings the evening to its emotional summit.\n\n**Tic
 ket link here:**\n\nhttps://torontosummermusic.com/event/heifetz-the-dolph
 in-strad/\n\nUse this code for 10% off your ADULT ticket price----CULTURE1
 0
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31383
 1824/
